            "sort": 1,
            "name": "Introduction",
            "value": "<p>While automobiles have become essential for daily commuting, professional activities, and social interactions, their unrestricted usage presents several challenges. This essay will examine some key problems arising from this trend and propose measures to address them.</p>",
            "question_id": 42100,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 3278,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p><strong>To begin with, excessive reliance on cars causes significant environmental and urban issues.</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(45, 194, 107);\"> First of all, the most pressing concern is air pollution, as vehicles emit harmful gases such as carbon dioxide and nitrogen oxides into the atmosphere. Consequently, this not only triggers respiratory diseases among city dwellers but also contributes to climate change on a global scale.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\">In addition to environmental degradation, another major problem is traffic congestion in metropolitan areas. During rush hours, roads become packed with vehicles, which means commuters often waste hours stuck in traffic jams. As a result, people experience heightened stress levels and reduced productivity, affecting both their work performance and overall well-being.</span></p>",
            "question_id": 42100,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 3279,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<p><strong>However, several solutions can be implemented to discourage excessive car use.</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(45, 194, 107);\">Most importantly, one effective approach would be for governments to invest heavily in public transportation systems. By expanding metro and bus networks and ensuring they run frequently and reliably, these services would become more convenient and attractive to commuters. This would, in turn, encourage people to opt for public transport rather than driving their own vehicles.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\">Furthermore, companies should adopt remote working policies wherever feasible. Allowing employees to work from home for several days a week would significantly reduce the need for daily commuting. Consequently, this would lead to fewer cars on the roads during peak hours, thereby alleviating both congestion and pollution issues simultaneously.</span></p>",
            "question_id": 42100,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
